      "description": "round=0 is every request's first call. round=N (N>0) only happens if the model needed another tool-calling round. A feature whose bars fall off a cliff after round 0-1 is settling fast; long tails mean the model is frequently needing several search attempts (see Scout Report's real example: two too-narrow searches before a widened one succeeded).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
